 "notes": [
  "The breadboard picture is drawn with rows j-f on the upper half and e-a on the lower half. Catalogue banks are 't' = rows a-e and 'b' = rows f-j, so I used the row letters from the picture. The upper half is bank 'b' and the lower half is bank 't'.",
  "The pushbutton straddles the centre gap at columns 4 and 6. Side 2 (2.l, 2.r) is column 4, which goes to 5V. Side 1 (1.l, 1.r) is column 6, which goes to pin 2 and the resistor. Which leg is 'l' or 'r' is assumed, because the legs in each pair are joined inside the part.",
  "The teal wire from pin 2 ends in row j of column 6, the same strip as the button leg.",
  "The picture shows the 10k resistor ending near column 8-9. I put its second lead in column 9, where the short black wire starts, so it connects. The rail hole numbers (bp.2, bp.4, bn.2, bn.9) are estimated from the picture.",
  "The black wire from the Arduino goes to the second GND pin on the power header, which I mapped to GND.2.",
  "The picture shows the 5V rail wire going to the lower '+' rail and the GND wire going to the '-' rail. The orange wire (column 4, row c) goes to the + rail (5V). The black wire (column 9, row b) goes to the - rail (GND)."
 ],
